summary: Powers itself off
description: |
    Powers itself off.

    This is intended to be used by the Guest in a Beaker job using a
    <guestrecipe>.
    When using it, the Guest powers off to allow the Host machine to safely
    modify the guest settings (such as VM configuration, firmware settings).
    The Host should then power it back on in a separate further task.

    See also: misc/wait-guest-poweroff
contact: Oliver Gutierrez <ogutierr@redhat.com>
component:
  - kernel
path: /misc/self-poweroff
test: bash -x ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
    - type: file
      pattern:
          - /cki_lib
duration: 1h
extra-summary: /misc/self-poweroff
extra-task: /misc/self-poweroff
